DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");
BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, -6, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 2, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, 1, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<2, 6, -7>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 0, -7>") . Compute("<10, -10, -4>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -8, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, 4>") . Compute("<1, -8, -5>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, -4, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, -3, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -5, -5, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-7, 0, 2>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -9, -4>") x Compute("<9, -8, 8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, -5, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, 9, 6>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 5, -10>") x Compute("<5, 9, -10>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, -5, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, -10, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, 5, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, 0, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 1, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, -4, 5>") . Compute("<7, 10, -9>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, 9, 1>") . Compute("<-9, -5, -8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, 10, -6>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -3, -10>") . Compute("<8, -6, 6>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -5, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, -3, -3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, 5, 1>") . Compute("<9, 10, 1>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 1, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, -1, -6>") . Compute("<-5, -9, 3>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -4, 3>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<6, -1, -4>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, -4, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, -3, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, -8, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 6, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, -6, -1>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 0, -8>") x Compute("<6, -8, 7>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, 7, -1>") . Compute("<-5, 8, 5>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 2, 3>") x Compute("<-7, -6, 0>")}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
